      hints: ["Say the counting row out loud.", "7 … and one more."],
      why: "Every number has a <b>next one</b> – counting never has to stop." },
    { q: "Count the dots: ●●●●●  ●●●  How many are there?",
      type: "number", answer: 8,
      hints: ["First group: 5. Second group: 3.", "5 … then 6, 7, 8."],
      why: "Counting in <b>groups</b> (5 and 3) is faster than one by one – your very first math trick!" },
    { q: "Which is MORE: 12 marbles or 9 marbles?",
      type: "choice", choices: ["12", "9", "both the same", "you can't tell"], answer: 0,
      hints: ["Which number comes later when you count up?", "9 … 10, 11, 12 – so 12 comes later."],
      why: "Later in the counting row = <b>more</b>. Numbers put the world in order." },
    { q: "One less than 10 = ?",
      type: "number", answer: 9,
      hints: ["Count backwards: 10 …", "One step back."],
      why: "Counting works <b>backwards</b> too – meet the number line, your friend for many years." }
  ]
},
