      why: "<b>Solid, liquid, gas</b> — the same particles, differently arranged." },
    { q: "Heating ice until it turns to water is called …",
      type: "choice", choices: ["melting","freezing","boiling","mixing"], answer: 0,
      hints: ["Solid to liquid.","Not all the way to steam."],
      why: "<b>Melting</b>: added heat lets locked particles start to flow." },
    { q: "In which state are particles packed tightly in a fixed shape?",
      type: "choice", choices: ["solid","liquid","gas","none"], answer: 0,
      hints: ["Holds its own shape.","Like a brick."],
      why: "In a <b>solid</b>, particles are locked in place — fixed shape and volume." },
    { q: "Water freezes at what temperature? (°C)",
      type: "number", answer: 0, unit: "°C",
      hints: ["The zero of the Celsius scale.","Ice point."],
      why: "Cooling to <b>0 °C</b> flips water from liquid to solid." }
  ]
},
